---
layout: base.njk
title: "Ian Allan: Venture designer, ethical technologist; East Coast, New Zealand."
excerpt: "The professional profile website of Ian Allan, and an ongoing experiment in rewilding the internet."
---
<header>
    {% include "navbar.njk" %}
    {% include "profile.njk" %}
    <div class="cta">
        <h1>Call-to-action</h1>
        <p class="copy">Use all my skills and insights to turn your ideas into valuable hi- and low-tech products and
            ventures.</p>
        <p class="button"><a class="button-inline" href="#services"><span class="bracket">[</span>Use me ↓<span class="bracket">]</span></a><span class="button-tag">
                (#services)</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero">
        <img class="me-image" src="images/me-poppy.jpg" alt="Me all poppy">
    </div>
</header>
<main>
    <section id="services" class="first">
        <h1>Services</h1>
        <p class="l1"><span class="highlight">Use me when you need:</span></p>
        {# Skill lists are real lists so each design can present them its own way.
           custom.css runs them back together as the semicolon-delimited sentence
           they've always been; pro.css lays them out as a grid. Left in sentence
           case for the OG reading — pro.css lifts the first letter of each. #}
        <div class="service">
            <h2>Venture design</h2>
            <ul class="skills">
                <li>Go-to-market scenarios</li>
                <li>productised ideas</li>
                <li>operationalised initiatives</li>
                <li>product-market analysis</li>
                <li>pricing strategies and modelling</li>
                <li>subsequent proposals, pitches, collateral, and websites</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="service">
            <h2>Technology design</h2>
            <ul class="skills">
                <li>Solution as product</li>
                <li>lean web solutions</li>
                <li>prototypes</li>
                <li>human-computer interaction</li>
                <li>UX/UI design</li>
                <li>appropriate technology decisions</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="service">
            <h2>Learning design</h2>
            <ul class="skills">
                <li>Programme-market analysis</li>
                <li>curriculum design</li>
                <li>authentic experiential assessments</li>
                <li>workshop design and delivery</li>
                <li>online learning design</li>
                <li>face-to-face teaching and learning</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        {# Wrapped so the Pro design can treat the question, its lead-in and the
           list as one panel. The OG design reads straight through the div. #}
        <div class="why">
            <p><span class="highlight">But why use me specifically?</span></p>
            <p class="l2">Because you'd love:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><span class="infotip"
                        data-tooltip="When you only have budget for one human, it pays to get a useful one.">All-in-one
                        technical, design, and executive skills</span><span class="tap-indicator"
                        aria-hidden="true">👈</span></li>
                <li><span class="infotip"
                        data-tooltip="On the list of very unsatisfying things, someone phoning in AI slop when you needed deep understanding is right up there.">Slop-free
                        writing and world-class production</span></li>
                <li><span class="infotip"
                        data-tooltip="A uniquely broad and deep and fast-paced career requiring mucking in and taking ownership and figuring it out. Often the hard way.">Intuition from decades of experiences</span></li>
                <li><span class="infotip"
                        data-tooltip="Astute observer of human behaviour and motivation, widely read, and attuned to long-term trends over short-term wins.">Insightful
                        market readings</span></li>
                <li><span class="infotip"
                        data-tooltip="Don't take my word for it, others hold my contributions in high regard.">A trusted
                        creative and critical voice</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section id="activities">
        <h1>Activities</h1>
        <p class="l1"><span class="highlight">What's happening:</span></p>
        {# Activity lists are real lists so each design can present them its own
           way. custom.css runs them back together as the comma-delimited
           sentences they've always been — ".no-stop" drops the closing full
           stop, ".and-last" puts "and" before the final item. pro.css lays them
           out as rows instead. #}
        <h2>Currently &amp; previously</h2>
        <ul class="activities">
            <li class="featured"><a href="https://saved.co.nz" target="_blank" class="popout tooltip" rel="noopener"
                    data-tooltip="A multi-phase service and challenger brand to provide ownership of &mdash; and training/certification in &mdash; resilient, sovereign, and price-sensitive tech."><strong>Saved</strong></a></li>
            <li><a href="https://ianallan.vote" target="_blank" class="popout tooltip" rel="noopener"
                    data-tooltip="I ran for council and, going from a standing start with no previous profile, this website (and my public performances) got me close.">Gisborne
                    District Council candidacy</a></li>
            <li><a href="#modal-learning" class="popup tooltip" rel="noopener"
                    data-tooltip="I've been advocating and implementing successful experiential assessments for learning.">learning
                    design</a></li>
            <li><a href="#modal-advocacy" class="popup tooltip" rel="noopener"
                    data-tooltip="AI will make public vocational education the most societally-valuable skill-builder.">vocational
                    education advocacy</a></li>
            <li><a href="#modal-exec" class="locked" rel="noopener"
                    data-tooltip="I provide intrapreneurial value to organisations: taking initiative to develop new ideas, products, or services">tech-exec
                    services</a></li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Emerging</h2>
        <ul class="activities">
            <li><a href="#modal-pockit" class="locked tooltip" rel="noopener"
                    data-tooltip="A multi-phase lifestyle product suite and brand to help us beat big tech and the smartphone.">Pockit</a>
            </li>
            <li><a href="#modal-sinkashi" class="locked tooltip" rel="noopener"
                    data-tooltip="A purposefully low-tech, mechanical, integrated, food scrap collector for people who hate collecting food scraps &mdash; most of us then.">Sinkashi</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Blogging</h2>
        {% set latestPosts = collections.blogWithNumbers | reverse %}
        <ul class="activities and-last">
            {% for post in latestPosts %}
            {% if loop.index <= 3 %}
            <li><a href="{{ post.url }}" class="tooltip" data-tooltip="{{ post.data.excerpt }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
            </li>
            {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            <li><a href="/blog">the rest</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</main>
{% include "modal-learning.njk" %}
{% include "modal-advocacy.njk" %}
{% include "modal-exec.njk" %}
{% include "modal-pockit.njk" %}
{% include "modal-saved.njk" %}
{% include "modal-sinkashi.njk" %}
